    "title": "Labor Department Inspector General to Review Economic Data Collection and Reporting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By PYMNTS ,\n4 hours ago In a letter addressed to William J. Wiatrowski, acting commissioner of the Bureau of Labor Statistics, Laura B. Nicolosi, assistant inspector general for audit, wrote that the review was triggered by the BLS’ announcement that it will reduce its data collection activities for the Consumer Price Index and the Producer Price Index, and the agency’s recent “large downward revision” of its estimate of new jobs in the Employment Situation Report. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
